diff --git a/docs/storage-usage.md b/docs/storage-usage.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b6f3224
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/storage-usage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Storage usage
+
+`Account#bytes_used` and `Board#bytes_used` read an indexed, background-maintained
+cache. They return zero until the first calculation and reflect changes after the
+storage worker runs (normally scheduled every minute). Reads do not enumerate
+attachments and do not memoize a potentially stale value on the model instance.
+
+We count each attachment's blob `byte_size` for:
+
+- Card images, including draft and closed cards
+- Embeds in board public descriptions
+- Embeds in card descriptions and comment bodies
+
+Avatars, unattached uploads, imports/exports, previews, variants, and remote URLs
+are excluded. Reusing a blob in different attachments counts each attachment;
+repeating it in the same rich text uses Action Text's single attachment.
+
+## Background processing
+
+Attachment transactions append `Storage::Entry` rows. They never update a shared
+account or board counter. Card moves and card/board deletions append zero-byte
+entries so the worker can reconcile ownership or remove cached usage.
+
+`Storage::AccountUsageJob` folds at most 1,000 entries into `Storage::Usage` rows
+per transaction, using bulk writes. Card subtotals remember their last counted
+board, so moving a card doesn't scan its attachments or comments. Account and
+board totals are adjusted from those subtotals and direct board attachment
+changes. Memory and query work are bounded by the batch, not the board's history.
+
+Workers serialize on the account's **cache row**, not its Account record. Cache
+writes and deletion of the exact processed entries share a transaction, making
+retries and overlapping jobs safe. Newly appended entries remain for the next
+batch. Signed deltas reconcile even when writers commit out of order; the public
+read methods never report a temporarily negative balance. Different accounts can
+run concurrently. The recurring sweep also recovers work if a job fails or
+continuation enqueueing is interrupted.
+
+Existing attachments are backfilled 100 at a time. The `storage_tracked` marker
+and its addition entry are committed together under an attachment lock; deletion
+atomically claims that marker before recording a subtraction. The marker is not
+exported, and backfill waits for imports to complete. Thus existing installations
+and imported accounts need no synchronous full-account recount.
+
+Run the worker queue and the recurring scheduler to keep usage current. A manual
+sweep can be queued with `Storage::Entry.process_all_later`.
+
+As with other callback-maintained application data, raw SQL changes and bulk
+attachment deletion bypass accounting. Use the normal attachment/model APIs for
+changes; bulk imports are supported explicitly through the backfill marker.
diff --git a/lib/rails_ext/active_storage_usage.rb b/lib/rails_ext/active_storage_usage.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cfce2c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/rails_ext/active_storage_usage.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+ActiveSupport.on_load(:active_storage_attachment) do
+  include Storage::Attachment
+end
+
+# Rails' detach-many implementation uses delete_all, bypassing the individual
+# attachment deletion path. Keep the blobs, but account for each detached file.
+module ActiveStorageDetachManyUsage
+  def detach
+    if attachments.any?
+      ActiveStorage::Attachment.transaction { attachments.each(&:delete) }
+      attachments.reset if attachments.respond_to?(:reset)
+      record.attachment_changes.delete(name)
+    end
+  end
+end
+
+Rails.application.config.to_prepare do
+  ActiveStorage::Attached::Changes::DetachMany.prepend ActiveStorageDetachManyUsage
+end
